tle":"Introduction","source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:65a3172c87c8787b8a09256bbdf0d2dde85a04a1428a7c4be69020061af911bf","file":"preprints/Pointwise-convergence-of-triple-ergodic-averages-for-mixing-transformations-October-4-2026/build/paper/sections/introduction.tex","line":21,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"0c70d8ae52f27e7d3448d22ad6ecb9b14b5107524fcba3744946b11a00759cf5","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Pointwise-convergence-of-triple-ergodic-averages-for-mixing-transformations-October-4-2026/build/paper/sections/introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:65a3172c87c8787b8a09256bbdf0d2dde85a04a1428a7c4be69020061af911bf","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Pointwise-convergence-of-triple-ergodic-averages-for-mixing-transformations-October-4-2026/build/paper/sections/introduction.tex#L21"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:main}\nLet $(X,\\mathcal F,\\mu)$ be an arbitrary probability space and let\n$T:X\\to X$ be an invertible mixing probability preserving transformation\nwith measurable inverse.  For every triple of bounded measurable functions\n$f_1,f_2,f_3:X\\to\\C$,\n\\[\n A_N(f_1,f_2,f_3)(x)\n \\longrightarrow \\prod_{j=1}^3\\int_X f_j\\,d\\mu\n \\quad\\text{for $\\mu$-almost every }x\n\\]\nas $N\\to\\infty$ through all positive integers.  The exceptional null set\nmay depend on the triple of functions."}
